Here's the formal audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` using the **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog**, with integration-test calibration applied.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch will never execute per run. If the data model changes, the untested branch silently hides a gap.  
**Integration calibration:** Not downgraded — conditional assertion logic is problematic at any scope.  
**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsStandardUser()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsPremiumUser_WithDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.15m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — one code path never verified.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** No assertion call. Passes even if inserts silently discard data. The method name implies "no exception" intent, but that isn't verified by the framework.  
**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — data corruption goes undetected.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hardcoded 3-second sleep introduces flakiness and slows the suite. On a slow CI agent, 3s may not be enough; on a fast machine, it's wasted time.  
**Integration calibration:** Downgraded from High → Medium (integration tests may need async coordination), but still a smell because a polling/signaling approach is available.  
**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of sleeping
    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the expected timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; 3s added to every run.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the stack trace points to a line but gives no semantic context.  
**Fix:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip correctly");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip correctly");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned on insert");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage — developers must open code to understand CI failures.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are **well-designed** and demonstrate good integration-test practice:

| Method | Why it's clean |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion verifying absence — precise |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is self-documenting after adding 3 items |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Tests a real concurrency concern with proper assertion |

The in-memory SQLite approach avoids **Mystery Guest** — the database is hermetic and test-scoped. The `[TestCategory("Integration")]` annotation is correct. No **General Fixture** issues — all fields are used by all tests.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Low | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Medium | Split into two focused test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Medium | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling loop |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Low | Add message strings to multi-assert methods |

Fixes #1 and #4 are ~2-minute changes. Fixes #2 and #3 require modest restructuring. Overall the suite is in **good shape** — 5 of 7 tests are clean, and the architectural choice of in-memory SQLite is solid.
